sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Customer
    participant Channel as Mobile/Web App
    participant WAF as WAF / DDoS Protection
    participant APIGW as API Gateway
    participant IAM as Customer IAM
    participant BFF as Digital API / BFF Layer
    participant TransferSvc as Transfer Service
    participant FraudRT as Real-Time Fraud Engine
    participant CBSGW as CBS Transaction Gateway
    participant CBS as COBOL CBS on z/OS
    participant Audit as Audit / Compliance Store
    participant EventBus as Durable Event Bus

    Customer->>Channel: Submit transfer request
    Channel->>WAF: HTTPS request
    WAF->>APIGW: Forward allowed request
    APIGW->>IAM: Validate identity, MFA, authorization
    IAM-->>APIGW: Authorized customer context
    APIGW->>BFF: Route transfer command
    BFF->>TransferSvc: Create transfer command
    TransferSvc->>TransferSvc: Validate command and idempotency key
    TransferSvc->>FraudRT: Evaluate real-time fraud risk

    alt Fraud detected
        FraudRT-->>TransferSvc: Reject / cancel transaction
        TransferSvc->>Audit: Record fraud decision
        TransferSvc-->>BFF: Transfer cancelled
        BFF-->>Channel: Inform customer
    else Fraud not detected
        FraudRT-->>TransferSvc: Approve risk decision
        TransferSvc->>CBSGW: Execute CBS transaction
        CBSGW->>CBS: Execute money movement
        CBS-->>CBSGW: Transaction result
        CBSGW->>Audit: Record CBS transaction audit
        CBSGW-->>TransferSvc: Transaction result
        TransferSvc->>EventBus: Publish transfer event
        TransferSvc-->>BFF: Transfer result
        BFF-->>Channel: Inform customer
    end
